1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,550
You felt your phone vibrate.

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:02,570
You checked it.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:03,410
Nothing.

4
00:00:04,020 --> 00:00:06,010
So what did you actually feel?

5
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:08,615
Sometimes the phone never vibrated at

6
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:08,990
all.

7
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:11,515
That experience is called a phantom

8
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:12,210
vibration.

9
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:15,435
One proposed explanation starts with what

10
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:16,050
you expect.

11
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:17,970
When you're waiting for a call,

12
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:20,175
your brain may interpret another sensation

13
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,730
as the familiar buzz.

14
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,355
Pressure from clothing or a small

15
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:26,350
muscle movement are possible candidates.

16
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:29,295
But researchers haven't pinned down exactly

17
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,690
what causes it.

18
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:33,110
Surveys document the experience.

19
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:34,890
They don't prove that mechanism.

20
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:37,775
So a convincing buzz isn't always

21
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,610
proof that your phone vibrated.

22
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:41,630
The sensation can feel real,

23
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:43,870
even when the alert wasn't.
